# Release setup trees staged into job dirs are release-specific and ~30 MB. The job's onboot.cmd
# is the artefact worth keeping; the payload is re-staged per release.
*/setup/
*/qubes-tools-*.exe

# PER-RUN ARTEFACTS prime-run.sh STAGES INTO A JOB DIR, which is a tracked tree in a public repo.
# JOBDIR="mgmt/prime-jobs/$JOB", and the run writes three kinds of file into it: a copy of
# _common/fix-guest-clock.ps1 (:181), the host's true-UTC stamp hoststamp.txt (:183), and one empty
# <name>.flag per --flag (:148). All three are rewritten by every prime and describe a guest that no
# longer exists. Two of them sat in `git status` of this repo until 2026-10-27, one `git add -A`
# from being published - which is the hazard the "never git add -A" rule exists to contain.
# The job's onboot.cmd stays tracked; it is the artefact worth keeping.
*/fix-guest-clock.ps1
!_common/fix-guest-clock.ps1
*/hoststamp.txt
*/*.flag
